  "description": "RONGOT crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P c a 21. Reported CIF formula moiety: C174 H150 N25 Ni4 O42 Y5 2+,N1 O3 1-,3(H2 O1),Cl1 1-. From the CIF bond table, Y1 (Y) has 7 O neighbors; Y2 (Y) has 8 O neighbors; Y3 (Y) has 7 O neighbors; Y4 (Y) has 7 O neighbors; Y5 (Y) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 3 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Ni4 (Ni) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 13 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.201-4.184 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 98.62-125.31°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ni4Y5(PhCOO)10(HL)4(HLzw)4(OH)2(NO3)1.5(H2O)0.5]0.5Cl(NO3)·3H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 0 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 0 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Ni(II), Y(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
